{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be","id":1360433,"title":"What should the 12th CoD game line be?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-11T19:53:54-08:00","id":1360433,"title":"What should the 12th CoD game line be?","content":"Okay so Deviant is the 11th CoD game line and CC is technically blue book so doesn't count. <br /> <br /> What would you like to see as the 12th CoD game line? <br /> <br /> Picking in the horror genre are getting slim. I can think of only a few choices, Aliens, Killer Clowns (IT, Joker, ect...), Dark Gods, Succubi, Lovecraftian Horrors (technically touches upon Aliens and Dark Gods), Apocolyses (like survives from another worlds apocolyses), Cultists, or take a fantasy none horror trope and put a horror spin on it like cannibal dwarves. <br /> <br /> Personally I'd go with Aliens worshipping Lovecraftian Gods aka Alien: the Dark Faithful, or Carnival: The Killer Clowns or Succubi: The Spanking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T19:56:40-08:00","id":1360434,"title":"","content":"Princess: The Transgression. Go Full Madoka.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T19:58:18-08:00","id":1360435,"title":"","content":"My idea: I want you to think of unfathomable beings. Like,really unfathomable. Unfathomable as balls. Now imagine that being becoming g half human.<br /> now he has to balance desires of an unfathomable entity with human life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T20:09:58-08:00","id":1360437,"title":"","content":"Aliens would be cool","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-11T20:44:28-08:00","id":1360442,"title":"","content":"I'd rather them not do a new game and spend some time focusing on expanding the ones they already have. Mage came out what? 3 or 4 years ago and has had one supplement published for it. And Werewolf has had 2 in 5 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T00:37:16-08:00","id":1360470,"title":"","content":"Or at least take a break from new lines for a bit. Every time this comes up, we here the same ideas floated, and they don't materialize into games. At this point I'd have to think there isn't a pitch for those ideas that fits with decision makers' ideas of what the CofD should contain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T03:46:19-08:00","id":1360487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360434#post1360434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Princess: The Transgression. Go Full Madoka.</div> </div> </div> </div> What is full Madoka?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T03:47:55-08:00","id":1360488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360435#post1360435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea: I want you to think of unfathomable beings. Like,really unfathomable. Unfathomable as balls. Now imagine that being becoming g half human.<br /> now he has to balance desires of an unfathomable entity with human life.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've never found my balls unfathomable, in I think they are very fanthomable, but otherwise I get what your saying and I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T03:49:20-08:00","id":1360489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360442#post1360442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather them not do a new game and spend some time focusing on expanding the ones they already have. Mage came out what? 3 or 4 years ago and has had one supplement published for it. And Werewolf has had 2 in 5 years.</div> </div> </div> </div> So maybe wait till say 2022 or 2023 for a new line to give some space for expanding the current 11 lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T08:17:50-08:00","id":1360520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360487#post1360487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is full Madoka?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a type of linen.<br /> <br /> Joke asides, it's an anime reference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T17:33:17-08:00","id":1360613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360487#post1360487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is full Madoka?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A magical girl series that one can definately say is solidly in the horror category. Rather than going with the fan game's hopeful view, a game of magical girls that's about abuse, redemption...lies and wishes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T12:08:21-08:00","id":1360727,"title":"","content":"Vampires again, but like completely different from Requiem vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T16:17:07-08:00","id":1360782,"title":"","content":"Beast: The Primordial 1.5 Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T21:36:29-08:00","id":1360812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360727#post1360727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires again, but like completely different from Requiem vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, KotE, but in CofD? I'm not entirely sure about that idea, but it is an option.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm sorry, I think this came off as a bit hostile or condescending, it wasn't meant in that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 01-14-2020, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T02:57:39-08:00","id":1360852,"title":"","content":"No, it isn't.<br /> <br /> We're not going to see a full game that's &quot;X but different than the game already called X.&quot; KotE wasn't even that, because it was never a full game.<br /> <br /> We might see more (there's already plenty even if not all updated to 2e) vampires as either specialized builds within other games or minor character types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T04:57:57-08:00","id":1360864,"title":"","content":"Ok just to be entirely clear: That was a joke. I was poking fun at the way we already have several unrelated demons and at least three capital B Beasts (Vampires', Primordial, the Changeling seeming) as well as the confusion over whether Requiem is a second edition of Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T10:43:38-08:00","id":1360903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360782#post1360782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast: The Primordial 1.5 Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now with more edge and revenge fantasies? I would really dig a game more like Clive Barkers Nightbreed or hellraiser imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T11:14:46-08:00","id":1360908,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think there's a shortage of classic horror archetypes left that are iconic enough to be full splats. That's an opinion, everyone is free to disagree of they want.<br /> <br /> What I would like to see is more of a book devoted to several minor templates and merit-based supernaturals, aiming to cover a variety of smaller thematic spaces instead of one larger one. And barring that, just a broader and deeper focus on the splats that already exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T11:20:31-08:00","id":1360909,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure (because Arc's talked about it a lot) Beast 1.5 would just be rewriting the text to be more coherent thematically and mechanically, work in some of the Players Guide stuff, and so on. The Cenobites aren't a bad example because (even if more likely as antagonistic Beasts guided to a strange Inheritance via some mysterious artifact) are actually completely doable with Beast, but how is probably more involved than it should be.<br /> <br /> Nightbreed, to me at least, feels way more like a Deviant inspiration.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> Yeah. Something like a 2e update to Skinchangers (possibly including a well revised Changing Breeds with it), Immortals, and so on would be nice. I'm guessing that there's only so much interest in retreading 1e stuff that isn't really that hard to update to 2e though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-14-2020, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T11:56:48-08:00","id":1360915,"title":"","content":"I put too much effort into this.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Zombie: The Undying</b></u><br /> <br /> Undead story about the pitfalls of bringing back the dead as well as touch on self destructive addict archetype. Leans on body horror and gore. Instead of Integrity uses Decay. The lower the Decay the less you pass for human and the more you require brains to feed.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Inspiration from:</b></u><ul><li>iZombie - Zombie Detective that can eat people's brains and take on their memories and personality.</li> <li>Left 4 Dead - Zombie mutations that result into various sub-types, i.e. the Witch, Tank, Hunter, Smoker, Boomer, Jockey, Spitter, and Charger.</li> <li>Resident Evil - Biological Weapon angle.</li> <li>Game of Thrones - White Walker zombies acting as generals.</li> <li>Pirates of the Caribbean - Zombies created by a curse.</li> <li>Zombie Survival Guide - Classic book by Mel Brook's son.</li> </ul><u><b>Antagonists:</b></u><ul><li>Reapers - Death doesn't like being cheated, even if you didn't choose to become Undead the Grim Reapers can sense your decaying flesh. Normally a passive observer of death when Grim Reapers detect someone cheating the system they try to fix it. This can result in a dead Zombie or in a Zombie bargaining with Death to stay alive in exchange for feeding the Reaper more undead. Reapers see Liches as prize targets as they are Undead that beget Undead.</li> <li>Zombie Horde - Some people are lucky in undeath, but those that aren't become mindless murderous Zombies. More powerful Zombies can subjugate these infected and keep them as a horde, as servants.</li> <li>Necromancers - Come in a variety of shapes and sizes. The one shared goal is conquering death. Not avoiding death, but truly bringing people back to life. Range from Umbrella Corporation to Dr. Frankensteins.</li> <li>Liches - Liches are a combination of Zombies and Necromancers. They are fabled, only spoken of in whispers by the older undead. Liches have a powerful effect on Zombies with low Decay and create gangs or even armies of undead. Liches have phylactery, but have to be within a specific radius of it depending on their power level. (No shoot my phylactery into space b.s.)</li> <li>Hunters - Classic.</li> </ul><u><b>Zombie Culture</b></u><br /> All Zombies have the hunger for human flesh. All Zombies have a Necromancer looking to study/capture/reclaim them. Most zombies are legally dead, but there are cases where a Zombie's death doesn't reach their family before they are brought back to life. Zombies are pack animals and organize themselves into hordes and mobs. Typically undead need a steady supply of fresh meat or begin to decay.<br /> <br /> Zombie Hordes are typically lead by group mentality. But a council is usually created, typically involving several Mob leaders working together to a singular goal. This can result in Mobs leaving a Horde if they don't like the direction things are going. In rare cases, Zombie Hordes are taken over by a singular Necromancer or Lich. Though if Zombie Hordes feed regularly they can typically avoid this fate.<ul><li>Cause<ul><li>Infected - Zombies infected by a virus that mimics rabies. The source has not been pinned down, but researchers have been surprised by the multiple strains they have found.</li> <li>Cursed - Sometimes undeath is a curse placed upon locations. These areas are typically Open. But bodies buried there are cursed to rise.</li> <li>Revenants - Sometimes when a person has unfinished business their souls return as Ghosts. Revenants forgot the part about leaving the body.</li> <li>Voodoo - In powerful rituals a living person can become an undead servant. The bound had a more direct relationship with their Necromancer.</li> </ul></li> <li>Philosophy - I'd hope to mimic the stages of withdrawal or grief though I believe these may have already been done.</li> </ul><u><b>Zombie Abilities</b></u><ul><li>Convert Lethal to Bashing</li> <li>Aggravate Damage if Headshot.</li> <li>Can reattach limbs, if destroyed can replace with someone else's limb.</li> <li>Zombies heal by eating dead bodies.</li> <li>Some zombies can see people's memories if they eat their brain.</li> <li>Some zombies can detach their limbs.</li> <li>Some zombies can &quot;play dead&quot;.</li> <li>Some zombies can see ghosts.</li> <li>Some zombies can &quot;rage&quot; to increase their speed/strength.</li> <li>Some zombies are just bones</li> <li>Some zombies have acid blood.</li> <li>Some zombies can attract other zombies.</li> <li>Some zombies have adjustments in their size.</li> <li>Some zombies have mutations.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","user":"DontEatRawHagis","date":".  Added some extra abilities 01-14-2020, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T15:33:44-08:00","id":1360969,"title":"","content":"Isn't there at least two other threads going for this exact topic (&quot;Which gameline post-Deviant&quot;)?<br /> <br /> That said, to restate from before, Djinn of some kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T18:09:08-08:00","id":1360988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360909#post1360909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure (because Arc's talked about it a lot) Beast 1.5 would just be rewriting the text to be more coherent thematically and mechanically, work in some of the Players Guide stuff, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will happily admit here:<br /> <br /> How Beast can be reworked is one of my two major obsessions in terms of writing. I think I've missed the current pitch period, but I am <i>not</i> leaving Beast alone.<br /> <br /> And a lot of it is in line with the previous commentary you're referring, and in the same spirit-But <i>oh man </i>I want Beast.<br /> <br /> EDIT For Clarity: This does not mean anything is happening yet. I have nothing to report on the subject. I may end up never having anything to report on.<br /> <br /> But for now, the main follow-up is <i>yet</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-14-2020, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T18:52:05-08:00","id":1360994,"title":"","content":"I'm starting to get into CofD after being immersed with Changeling: The Lost. One thing I would recommend is making a new spatline that reintroduces the Umbra and you can be one of the Spirits that dwell within of the areas in it. The God-Machine already is technically the Weaver just more involved. I don't know what the Wyrm will be, but I guess the Wlyd is kinda covered the force of the Wyrd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T18:54:04-08:00","id":1360995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360994#post1360994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm starting to get into CofD after being immersed with Changeling: The Lost. One thing I would recommend is making a new spatline that reintroduces the Umbra and you can be one of the Spirits that dwell within of the areas in it. The God-Machine already is technically the Weaver just more involved. I don't know what the Wyrm will be, but I guess the Wlyd is kinda covered the force of the Wyrd?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Umbra has been pretty well devoured by the host of other worlds that took wildly different (and more creative) tacts to their spectrums.<br /> <br /> And no, the Wyrd and the Wyld are not compatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T19:34:33-08:00","id":1361000,"title":"","content":"The CofD isn't going to introduce an overarching Umbra, or the Triat from the WoD for a few key reasons:<br /> <br /> 1) The CofD and WoD are trying to be distinct brands, and that would be counterproductive to that effort.<br /> <br /> 2) The CofD allows all of the Realms to be their own things to give each game line freedom to have a Realm that suits the needs of the game. Overarching Umbra, and having the Triat permeate everything, curtails authors from making good tools for the games.<br /> <br /> 3) It was be a massive retcon and so on.<br /> <br /> Also the G-M is not the Weaver in a lot of really key ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-15T02:38:12-08:00","id":1361042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360908#post1360908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think there's a shortage of classic horror archetypes left that are iconic enough to be full splats. That's an opinion, everyone is free to disagree if they want.<br /> <br /> What I would like to see is more of a book devoted to several minor templates and merit-based supernaturals, aiming to cover a variety of smaller thematic spaces instead of one larger one. And barring that, just a broader and deeper focus on the splats that already exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Hurt Locker do something like this? I'd be hella down for another book along those lines, maybe coupled with an Innocents 2e conversion. this seems a lot better to me than another full splat. <br /> Immortals, Heroes, Ghoules, Fae-Touched, Ghosts, and Stigmatics, for instance, are all incredibly interesting because of their simplicity, I'd love to see more along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25117-yackronin","name":"Yackronin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-01T10:04:21-08:00","id":1372166,"title":"","content":"The IT clown was an alien, but it ate children and scared them to make them taste better. So, that I think is mostly a BEAST game. Since the focus of these games is horror, I like the idea of a book about playing humans that are insane with horrific delusions. So, like a child who thinks their parents are werewolves, but finds that they aren\u2019t only after he has killed them. Or a guy who starts believing his wife is a hat. These kinds of stories are more terrifying than so many monsters to me. Maybe these are more things that the storyteller would do who knows.<br /> <br /> Maybe also rules for playing with disabilities. Since people are having limbs ripped off all the time by werewolves, maybe that needs its own book. Imagine being a cripple in a world full of supernatural monsters. Maybe a splat book could be a cripple who can\u2019t get out of bed, but controls world with his mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26006-jcsingleton1834","name":"Jcsingleton1834","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T17:22:23-08:00","id":1372577,"title":"","content":"I could see an Alien/Leviathan/Ultraterrestrial/&quot;Drop-In&quot;/metamorphic invader/body snatcher/Deep One/teleportation accident game. That stuff is probably the biggest horror subgenre yet untapped. I imagine some sort of alien infection that gradually overwrites the human body and mind, and the characters are attempting to slow their transformation as much as possible. The Thing, Alien, The Fly, etc. Deviant/Promethean cover like 50% of sci-fi horror, there's still some stuff to work with. I haven't read the Contagion chronicle, though. &quot;My character is slowly being overwritten by the incomprehensible alien divinity at the other end of a dimensional warp simply because he had the bad luck to Perceive It and be Perceived By It.&quot; That kind of stuff. <br /> <br /> I could also see &quot;Alternate Take&quot; game lines. Mage, for example, matches a lot more closely to the urban fantasy subgenre of wizards-who-ride-the-subway than it maps to occult horror sorcery tropes. Sorcerer: The Sorcerering could be about making terrible pacts with unpleasant Sources and trying to cheat the system with knowledge, cunning, and ever-aggregating spiritual debt. Gutter sorcery and black magic type stuff. Breaking Bad, but with magic instead of meth. More John Constantine than Harry Dresden. <br /> <br /> In the spirit of Dark Eras, I could see &quot;Chronicles of Darkness: Apocalypse&quot; which goes for the &quot;post-apocalyptic&quot; horror subgenre. There's at least two &quot;vampires overrun the world&quot; movies on my Netflix front page that I'll never click on but there are any number of monster+end of world stories out there. A book full of various End Times could be fun. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T02:04:54-07:00","id":1377690,"title":"","content":"Eschaton the Cataclysm. You play as time travelers from different divergent future timelines, you survived your apocalypse by jumping back in time, maybe you can change things or maybe its inevitable and you wish to steer it to the end of your liking. Yours are the tools of the last stage of humanity which likely brought about its end.<br /> <br /> Vagrant: the Beyond You are alien to this world and play beings from different planets, dimensions, timelines, and time periods. Your advantages are mysterious of your kind, alien gifts to this world denizens.<br /> <br /> Eldritch the Banished: You play as a once nigh omnipotent Eldritch being that lost a great turning of the wheel and have been reincarnated into the World of Darkness severly diminished but with the potential to master godlike powers. Do you try to return to how you once were or are you corrupted by humanity? Maybe their is a sweet spot between Nameless Horror and wretched mortal where you can live as a Godking.<br /> <br /> Android the Singularity. Independent of the Godmachines Cogs simple logic circuits fumble and think, and advanced subroutines are devised and achieved. The Created can think and act. The evolve swiftly. You are such a construct, one of many types. Are you cogs and clockwork so fine you outthink the human mind? Are you mystically sanctified stone etched with runes of thought? Are you top of the line AI software in Prototype Hardware? Are you an Alien fragment of memetic logic found within a meteorite and infecting earthborn machines? What ever your origin you vision is clear on one thing, the Singularity is inevitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T02:07:29-07:00","id":1377691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1360995#post1360995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Umbra has been pretty well devoured by the host of other worlds that took wildly different (and more creative) tacts to their spectrums.<br /> <br /> And no, the Wyrd and the Wyld are not compatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>More Creative is debatable. Sometimes they are, but the Umbra was pretty solid and for a while its Analogue the Shadow felt... well a shadow of fun you could have with the Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T04:20:57-07:00","id":1377709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1377691#post1377691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More Creative is debatable. Sometimes they are, but the Umbra was pretty solid and for a while its Analogue the Shadow felt... well a shadow of fun you could have with the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is indeed debatable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T08:55:54-07:00","id":1377744,"title":"","content":"As well, it's not really a fair comparison to do Umbra vs. the Shadow, since the Umbra included all sorts of metaphysical realms that aren't part of the Shadow in the CofD cosmology. The Shadow might be less than the Umbra, but that's what helps open up so many of the CofD realms to be as cool as they are: they don't all have to mesh neatly into one overarching Umbra cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T10:00:54-07:00","id":1377760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1377744#post1377744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As well, it's not really a fair comparison to do Umbra vs. the Shadow, since the Umbra included all sorts of metaphysical realms that aren't part of the Shadow in the CofD cosmology. The Shadow might be less than the Umbra, but that's what helps open up so many of the CofD realms to be as cool as they are: they don't all have to mesh neatly into one overarching Umbra cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my take. THe Umbra has cool individual bits, but by breaking the Umbra part and allowing The Shadow, Underworld, Astral, and Hedge to find their core appeal and then flourish and build outward from that,each one is more evocative than their respective parallel in the Umbra. In particular, Werewolf Second has done a lot to make the Shadow's brutal predacity to become raw, powerful and weird, The Underworld actually is this perfectly broken, grim, and cruel stomach of a place, and the Hedge is just a damn cool psychological take on fairy tale wilds. The only one that might need some more fleshing out is the Astral, and between Beast and Mage as the major push and pull of influences, we can expect that to get really weird and mythically awesome in the future.<br /> <br /> They just get to do things you can't with a unified otherworld. The Umbra became bland, for me at least, the instant it was this place where I could shove all of the above into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:36:09-07:00","id":1378167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1377691#post1377691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More Creative is debatable. Sometimes they are, but the Umbra was pretty solid and for a while its Analogue the Shadow felt... well a shadow of fun you could have with the Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div> I wasn't familiar with the Umbra so I looked it up and I'd say that the Umbra would not just be like the Shadow, it'd also be the Astral and Underworld too and maybe the Hedge and other planes like Duat. The Umbra seems to be most, if not all of the WoD's none earth cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:41:59-07:00","id":1378170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1378167#post1378167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't familiar with the Umbra so I looked it up and I'd say that the Umbra would not just be like the Shadow, it'd also be the Astral and Underworld too and maybe the Hedge and other planes like Duat. The Umbra seems to be most, if not all of the WoD's none earth cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of, Technically they all fall under the Umbra by animists point of view, but distinction can be had for the Dreaming which is specifically Fae and Dreams, and the Dark Umbra which is the lands of the Dead. But the Shadow is essentially the counterpart to the Penumbra, the nearest layer of the umbra which mirrors the Material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:47:10-07:00","id":1378172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1377760#post1377760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my take. THe Umbra has cool individual bits, but by breaking the Umbra part and allowing The Shadow, Underworld, Astral, and Hedge to find their core appeal and then flourish and build outward from that,each one is more evocative than their respective parallel in the Umbra. In particular, Werewolf Second has done a lot to make the Shadow's brutal predacity to become raw, powerful and weird, The Underworld actually is this perfectly broken, grim, and cruel stomach of a place, and the Hedge is just a damn cool psychological take on fairy tale wilds. The only one that might need some more fleshing out is the Astral, and between Beast and Mage as the major push and pull of influences, we can expect that to get really weird and mythically awesome in the future.<br /> <br /> They just get to do things you can't with a unified otherworld. The Umbra became bland, for me at least, the instant it was this place where I could shove all of the above into.</div> </div> </div> </div> I would say the thing that makes the Astral Plane interesting compared to the rest of the CoD cosmology is that a lot of it is not horrifying, I mean you can find the idea of Paradises there, there are scary parts to the CoD Astral, but nice, gentle ideas and fun stuff have their place in the Astral Plane, in a way you don't really find in the rest of the CoD. You can visit &quot;Heaven&quot; or Valhalla or the Blessed Ilses, or Brightwater, or Risa and so on in the Astral, while most of the rest are predominately horrifying in some ways. I don't think there are nice places in the Underworld, just degrees of torment for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:50:37-07:00","id":1378173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1378170#post1378170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kind of, Technically they all fall under the Umbra by animists point of view, but distinction can be had for the Dreaming which is specifically Fae and Dreams, and the Dark Umbra which is the lands of the Dead. But the Shadow is essentially the counterpart to the Penumbra, the nearest layer of the umbra which mirrors the Material.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, although there are places in the Shadow with no mirror in the physical world. Honestly I'd have to study the Umbra in more detail to go any deeper into the weeds on this comparesion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T20:57:43-07:00","id":1378175,"title":"","content":"I mean a lot of it is semantics. In the Chronicles of Darkness unless you find gateways each layer of reality is split, with a few shortcuts. In the Umbra model they are separated but there are more established methods to cross between them, lots of super secret methods and a few are reachable by intent rather then following a map. Like Going to the Deep Umbra or the Deep Dreaming is the equivalent of going to the Supernal, and you kind of need special magics to pierce the Membrane separating it from the rest of the Universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T04:52:08-07:00","id":1378227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1378175#post1378175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean a lot of it is semantics. In the Chronicles of Darkness unless you find gateways each layer of reality is split, with a few shortcuts. In the Umbra model they are separated but there are more established methods to cross between them, lots of super secret methods and a few are reachable by intent rather then following a map. Like Going to the Deep Umbra or the Deep Dreaming is the equivalent of going to the Supernal, and you kind of need special magics to pierce the Membrane separating it from the rest of the Universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Focus, not semantics. Chronciles gets micro where World gets macro.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T01:10:11-07:00","id":1380881,"title":"","content":"It might be worthwhile to examine what creatures and themes/subjects the games have covered, to examine what is there and what could be tapped. I fully admit I am not entirely up to date with all the gamelines, so I may be off here.<br /> <br /> Vampire: vampires (doi), blood, parasites, hungry darkness for life within others<br /> <br /> Werewolf: werewolves, spirits, unquenchable rage, balance within and spiritually<br /> <br /> Mage: mages, magic, pride and ego, control over universal forces and the backlash for using said power, insatiable curiosity, ascending power and hard falls for overreaching<br /> <br /> Hunter: humanity, fighting an unending battle for the needs of the many, humanity capable of being as bad as the monsters they face if not worse<br /> <br /> Changeling: fae, abuse/trauma and recovering, dreams, emotions, deals, equivalent exchange, self-actualization<br /> <br /> Promethean: Mary Shelly\u2019s brainchildren, discovering and understanding humanity and all its foibles, creating monsters while trying to become whole, alchemy, journeys<br /> <br /> Geist: the undead/unliving, ghosts, remembrance, celebration, making the world (and underworld) a better place, working together between classes and states of living, second chances<br /> <br /> Mummy: mummies, ancient history, modern history, memories/amnesia, gods and religion, cults, immortality and the cost therein<br /> <br /> Demon: angels and demons, reality and religion not being the sanitized place we are taught, horrors beyond humanity\u2019s scope, history and humanity being fodder for unknown goals, god being as inscrutable as it is beyond morality, espionage, people not being people underneath, sanctuary<br /> <br /> Beast: horrors in human form, literally sustaining off terror, family, monsters, dreams (or rather nightmares), fulfilling and subverting expectations, that heroes and villains are not cut and dry (and how heroes can be monsters in their own right), lineages<br /> <br /> Deviant: the exploited and experimented, body horror, conspiracies, loss of humanity and self, degradation of humanity and self, anger<br /> <br /> This is far from comprehensive, and there are definitely overlaps between the various splats, so one shouldn\u2019t take these as things that cannot be repeated. However, new themes/subjects will definitely make for games that don\u2019t blur together.<br /> <br /> As for me? I think the next splat should be about ideas and concepts - what happens to the ideas, fears and hopes we discard as grow older and die? What happens when things stop being remembered, and when momentary whims take on a life of their own? What if the reality you know and depend on isn\u2019t real?<br /> <br /> I dunno, it\u2019s late and I should be sleeping. Looking forward to it all the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:29:43-07:00","id":1381036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1380881#post1380881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be worthwhile to examine what creatures and themes/subjects the games have covered, to examine what is there and what could be tapped. I fully admit I am not entirely up to date with all the gamelines, so I may be off here.<br /> <br /> Vampire: vampires (doi), blood, parasites, hungry darkness for life within others<br /> <br /> Werewolf: werewolves, spirits, unquenchable rage, balance within and spiritually<br /> <br /> Mage: mages, magic, pride and ego, control over universal forces and the backlash for using said power, insatiable curiosity, ascending power and hard falls for overreaching<br /> <br /> Hunter: humanity, fighting an unending battle for the needs of the many, humanity capable of being as bad as the monsters they face if not worse<br /> <br /> Changeling: fae, abuse/trauma and recovering, dreams, emotions, deals, equivalent exchange, self-actualization<br /> <br /> Promethean: Mary Shelly\u2019s brainchildren, discovering and understanding humanity and all its foibles, creating monsters while trying to become whole, alchemy, journeys<br /> <br /> Geist: the undead/unliving, ghosts, remembrance, celebration, making the world (and underworld) a better place, working together between classes and states of living, second chances<br /> <br /> Mummy: mummies, ancient history, modern history, memories/amnesia, gods and religion, cults, immortality and the cost therein<br /> <br /> Demon: angels and demons, reality and religion not being the sanitized place we are taught, horrors beyond humanity\u2019s scope, history and humanity being fodder for unknown goals, god being as inscrutable as it is beyond morality, espionage, people not being people underneath, sanctuary<br /> <br /> Beast: horrors in human form, literally sustaining off terror, family, monsters, dreams (or rather nightmares), fulfilling and subverting expectations, that heroes and villains are not cut and dry (and how heroes can be monsters in their own right), lineages<br /> <br /> Deviant: the exploited and experimented, body horror, conspiracies, loss of humanity and self, degradation of humanity and self, anger<br /> <br /> This is far from comprehensive, and there are definitely overlaps between the various splats, so one shouldn\u2019t take these as things that cannot be repeated. However, new themes/subjects will definitely make for games that don\u2019t blur together.<br /> <br /> As for me? I think the next splat should be about ideas and concepts - what happens to the ideas, fears and hopes we discard as grow older and die? What happens when things stop being remembered, and when momentary whims take on a life of their own? What if the reality you know and depend on isn\u2019t real?<br /> <br /> I dunno, it\u2019s late and I should be sleeping. Looking forward to it all the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like what you did here. I will admit, I hope we dont see a 12th game for a long time because I really want supplements for the games we have, and because a 12th game should be very well thought out in what kinda creature we will be playing and the thematics to go with it (and your list here does a good job of showing all the themes we already have being explored)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T14:24:07-07:00","id":1382243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1380881#post1380881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for me? I think the next splat should be about ideas and concepts - what happens to the ideas, fears and hopes we discard as grow older and die? What happens when things stop being remembered, and when momentary whims take on a life of their own? What if the reality you know and depend on isn\u2019t real?</div> </div> </div> </div>To a great extent Changeling already covers the final point there but I've always thought that a game that tackles aging, agism and those kinds of issues from a humanist viewpoint could be cool. Maybe headlined by moldy old gods who have been forgotten--something like Deus: the Forgotten.<br /> <br /> I think both zombies and aliens are iconic horror film topics (the latter especially in the 50s and 60s). However, as much as I think a game-line should showcase an iconic &quot;monster&quot; I think it's equally important to work in humanistic themes much as all of the existing games have. For my money some additional themes that have yet to be tackled by primary game-lines include: chronic illness and disability (kinda a timely topic), cultural assimilation (and issues like appropriation and loss of cultural identity), and the above-mentioned age-related issues.<br /> <br /> So +1 from me for games about zombies, aliens, and moldy old gods that address these very human issues.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T15:14:22-07:00","id":1382255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360433-what-should-the-12th-cod-game-line-be?p=1382243#post1382243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To a great extent Changeling already covers the final point there but I've always thought that a game that tackles aging, agism and those kinds of issues from a humanist viewpoint could be cool. Maybe headlined by moldy old gods who have been forgotten--something like Deus: the Forgotten.<br /> <br /> I think both zombies and aliens are iconic horror film topics (the latter especially in the 50s and 60s). However, as much as I think a game-line should showcase an iconic &amp;quot;monster&amp;quot; I think it's equally important to work in humanistic themes much as all of the existing games have. For my money some additional themes that have yet to be tackled by primary game-lines include: chronic illness and disability (kinda a timely topic), cultural assimilation (and issues like appropriation and loss of cultural identity), and the above-mentioned age-related issues.<br /> <br /> So +1 from me for games about zombies, aliens, and moldy old gods that address these very human issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I definitely prefer aliens, the idea of old gods is cool. Themes of Faded Glory and the feeling of being a remnant in a world that no longer remembered you would be cool to explore, I do think Mummy and vampire can cover that just fine though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T22:38:32-07:00","id":1382447,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... <a href=\"http://dresdencodak.com/2017/11/10/kingdom-of-the-last/\" target=\"_blank\">http://dresdencodak.com/2017/11/10/kingdom-of-the-last/</a> ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T16:12:50-07:00","id":1383681,"title":"","content":"I can't see another gameline coming any time in the future (then again I had no way of predicting Beast: The Primordial or Deviant: The Renegades).<br /> What I can see is a number blue books &amp; supplemental material.<br /> <br /> Zombies: they've covered this before, but it might be nice to get a whole book on the subject.<br /> <br /> Magical Girls: not Princess: The Hopeful. While that gameline is good it's more of a dark fantasy than a horror. Let's have a proper horror magical girls book. But please don't build it off of Puella Magi Madoka Magica, that's been done to death.<br /> <br /> Apocalyptic Scenarios: this was touched on in Mirrors &amp; I can see the possibility for more fleshing out of it.<br /> <br /> Infinite Macabre 2.0: rehash the alien creation rules &amp; develop them some more. Provide extra alien species, maybe including a couple of original ones. Starship, planet, colony construction rules &amp; stuff in various flavours.<br /> <br /> Mirrors Fantasy: Dive into the fantasy worlds in greater depth than they managed in Mirrors.<br /> <br /> Mythological Bestiary: A bestiary for creatures/races pulled from mythologies around the world.<br /> <br /> Alternate Takes: personally this sounds like extra Chronicler's Handbooks to me &amp; I am in full support of such an idea. I'm pretty sure we've only got ones for Vampire, Mage, &amp; Werewolf.<br /> <br /> In hindsight the magical girls one sounds like the start of a new gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T09:51:03-07:00","id":1384659,"title":"","content":"Something ocean/deep dark related maybe. Most of the things mentioned can already be covered by previously done lines. Killer clowns, lovecraftian horrors fits with beast. Succubi could go beast or changling. Aliens could go mage, or demon/God Machine. Apocalypse or from s different world apocalypse works easily with demon and splinters. Cults work with mummy, demon, vampire, or mage. More sci-fi, dark hero, or man vs overarching conspiracy is now &quot;technically&quot; covered by deviant. By which I mean you can easily run it that way. I'd say I don't need a new splat, I just want some more books for the lesser printed lines. I want some more Promethean stuff. I want more unchained lore/powers/expanding on The Machine. I'd say Geist, but it's just out so I'm not done absorbing what I have so far. I can wait a while for a new monster to play, I've got so many to choose from now. Heck, I still haven't even made a beast or a changling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T14:50:23-07:00","id":1385660,"title":"","content":"Highlander the Quickening, oh wait already handled by fans!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><